{
  "sn35.132:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.132 ",
  "sn35.132:0.2": "13. Householders ",
  "sn35.132:0.3": "With Lohicca ",
  "sn35.132:1.1": "At one time Venerable Mahākaccāna was staying in the land of the Avantis in a wilderness hut near Makkarakaṭa. ",
  "sn35.132:1.2": "Then several students, pupils of the brahmin Lohicca, approached Mahākaccāna’s wilderness hut while collecting firewood. They walked and wandered all around the hut, making a colossal racket and all kinds of jeers: ",
  "sn35.132:1.3": "“These shavelings, fake ascetics, primitives, black spawn from the feet of our kinsman, the Lord! They’re honored, respected, revered, venerated, and esteemed by so-called inheritors of Vedic culture.” ",
  "sn35.132:1.4": "Then Mahākaccāna left his dwelling and said to those young students, ",
  "sn35.132:1.5": "“Young students, stop being so noisy. ",
  "sn35.132:1.6": "I will speak to you on the teaching.” ",
  "sn35.132:1.7": "When this was said, the young students fell silent. ",
  "sn35.132:1.8": "Then Mahākaccāna recited these verses for them: ",
  "sn35.132:2.1": "“For the brahmins of old, ethics were the highest; ",
  "sn35.132:2.2": "they remembered the ancient legends. ",
  "sn35.132:2.3": "Their sense doors were guarded, well protected, ",
  "sn35.132:2.4": "and they had mastered anger. ",
  "sn35.132:3.1": "Those brahmins who remembered <j>the ancient legends ",
  "sn35.132:3.2": "enjoyed virtue and absorption. ",
  "sn35.132:4.1": "But these have lost their way. <j>Saying